-- The MEF Body Systems Survey's coach association library.
--
-- COACH ONLY, PERMANENTLY. Migration 220 gives this table a coach and
-- platform administrator select policy and no member policy at all, so a
-- member session asking for these rows directly gets none. The app draws
-- the same fence a second time in lib/body-systems/associations.ts, which
-- is never imported by anything a member renders, and
-- tests/body-systems-member-language.test.ts proves the import graph.
--
-- POSSIBILITIES, NEVER CONCLUSIONS. Every association_text below is the
-- coach approved sentence, whole, including its cautious frame. The app
-- composes nothing around it: what a coach reads is exactly this column.
-- That is what makes the banned conclusion vocabulary enforceable, and
-- tests/body-systems-associations.test.ts reads these rows through the
-- renderer and fails on has, shows, indicates or confirms.
--
-- EVERY ENTRY DEFINES ITS TRIGGER PRECISELY, and every fired entry cites
-- the member's actual answers that fired it. The trigger vocabulary is
-- documented on the table in migration 220. "Elevated" means Often or
-- Almost always, which is body_systems_scale_options.is_elevated rather
-- than a number repeated in thirty eight triggers. "Cluster" means two or
-- more elevated inside the listed set.
--
-- WHERE A TRIGGER READS NARROWER THAN THE PROSE, it is because the prose
-- named an emphasis rather than a requirement, and the safest literal
-- reading was taken. Both cases are listed in the build report:
--   K-1 fires on K1 and K2 elevated. B9 strengthens it in the prose
--       ("especially with") and is not required.
--   K-2 fires on K4 elevated. Its second clause ("or K3 elevated
--       alongside it") also requires K4, so K4 is the trigger.

on conflict (entry_code) do nothing;
